      "body": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/20501#issuecomment-4173745103\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\nWhen using the FlashInfer backend, replace the separate temperature division, softmax, and copy-back with FlashInfer’s fused temperature-aware softmax. This should reduce kernel launches and intermediate memory traffic while preserving the existing behavior of all other branches, including the deterministic path.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n```\r\n            is_cuda()\r\n            and get_exec().kernel.sampling_backend == \"flashinfer\"\r\n            and not self.enable_deterministic\r\n```\r\nin this case, enable flashinfer softmax.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\npytest -q -p no:cacheprovider test/registered/sampling/test_sampling_mask.py test/registered/sampling/test_original_logprobs.py\r\n\r\nreturned logprobs allclose (atol 1e-5); sampled token ids identical in at least 99.9% of rows under the same seed flashinfer sampling consumes the same RNG offsets; mismatches only at ulp-level ties\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\n| arm | n | median | unit | hardware |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| baseline | 8 | 697.36 | us per Sampler.forward call (CUDA events) | NVIDIA B300 SXM6 PC x1 |\r\n| candidate | 8 | 414.765 | us per Sampler.forward call (CUDA events) | NVIDIA B300 SXM6 PC x1 |\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36081230057](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36081230057)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36081230017](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36081230017)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36081230305](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36081230305)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
